{"id":"activity_oscar_calf_rolling","name":"Calf Rolling","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Self-myofascial release","domain":"fitness","type":"canonical","verb":"Roll","lane_subcategory":"Rest","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Rolling the calf muscle from the ankle toward the knee.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Position the calf","instruction":"Sit with one calf on a roller or ball, hands behind you."},{"order":2,"title":"Roll the length","instruction":"Roll from just above the ankle toward just below the knee."},{"order":3,"title":"Rotate the leg","instruction":"Turn the leg slightly in and out to reach the sides."},{"order":4,"title":"Switch","instruction":"Repeat with the other calf."}],"instructions":"1. Sit with one calf on a roller or ball, hands behind you.\n2. Roll from just above the ankle toward just below the knee.\n3. Turn the leg slightly in and out to reach the sides.\n4. Repeat with the other calf.","safety_notes":"Use light-to-moderate pressure, never directly on a joint or bone. Move slowly and stop if it is sharply painful.","contraindications":["Blood clot or circulation problems, or taking blood thinners, unless your clinician has cleared it","Open wounds, bruising, rash or skin infection at the spot","Sharp, shooting or nerve-type pain (stop; use a lighter touch or skip it)"],"benefits":{"primary":"Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","secondary":["Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"]},"health_benefits":["Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"],"tags":["oscar patel","fascia","self-massage"],"body_parts":["calves"],"equipment_needed":["ball or foam roller"],"equipment":["ball or foam roller"],"recommended_duration":"30 seconds per side","recommended_frequency":"Daily or as needed","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":308},
{"id":"activity_oscar_cheek_puff_and_suck","name":"Cheek Puff and Suck","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Tongue and swallowing","domain":"grooming","type":"canonical","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Alternately puffing the cheeks out and drawing them in.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Breathe in","instruction":"Breathe in through your nose."},{"order":2,"title":"Puff the cheeks","instruction":"Puff your cheeks out with the lips closed."},{"order":3,"title":"Draw them in","instruction":"Close the lips and gently draw the cheeks inward."},{"order":4,"title":"Hold","instruction":"Hold for 2–3 seconds."},{"order":5,"title":"Release","instruction":"Release with a soft pop."}],"instructions":"1. Breathe in through your nose.\n2. Puff your cheeks out with the lips closed.\n3. Close the lips and gently draw the cheeks inward.\n4. Hold for 2–3 seconds.\n5. Release with a soft pop.","safety_notes":"Use gentle effort; stop if you feel dizzy or your jaw or ears hurt.","contraindications":["Dental work, braces or jaw (TMJ) pain: check with your dentist first","Difficulty swallowing or a choking risk","Oral injury, ulcers or infection","Under 18 unless a clinician has prescribed it"],"benefits":{"primary":"Trains the cheek and lip muscles","secondary":["Lip seal"]},"health_benefits":["Trains the cheek and lip muscles","Lip seal"],"tags":["oscar patel","myofunctional","tongue","cheeks","lips"],"body_parts":["mouth","tongue","jaw","lips"],"recommended_duration":"10 reps with a 2–3 second hold","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Tongue and swallowing exercises taught by a clinician have trial evidence for sleep apnea (systematic review linked); the claim that tongue posture reshapes adult facial bone is not supported by good evidence. Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 