{"id":"activity_oscar_chin_mentalis_taping","name":"Chin / mentalis taping","category":"Recovery","domain":"grooming","verb":"Tape","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":false,"intensity":"low","description":"Tape used around the chin during relaxation or sleep, retained as research-only source material and not enabled for self-guided use.","duration_minutes":1,"default_duration_min":1,"safety_notes":"Not available as a self-guided activity. Requires dental or orthodontic review before any implementation. Do not tape the mouth shut during sleep, especially with snoring, nasal obstruction or possible sleep apnea. Long-term facial reshaping through tape is not established.","contraindications":["Under 18","Dental work or orthodontics","TMJ symptoms","Oral injury or infection","Recent facial surgery"],"tags":["oscar patel","taping","research-only"],"body_parts":["face","jaw"],"tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; nothing here is a recommendation to try it.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":393},
{"id":"activity_oscar_comfortable_nasal_breathing","name":"Comfortable Nasal Breathing","category":"Breathwork","subcategory":"Breathwork","domain":"wellness","type":"canonical","verb":"Breathe","lane_subcategory":"Breathwork","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Breathing gently through the nose when the airway is clear.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Check the airway","instruction":"Make sure your nose is clear and breathing through it feels easy."},{"order":2,"title":"Close the lips gently","instruction":"Close your lips softly without pressing them together."},{"order":3,"title":"Breathe quietly","instruction":"Breathe in and out through your nose at an easy pace."},{"order":4,"title":"Stop if blocked","instruction":"If your nose is blocked or breathing feels hard, return to easy mouth breathing and see a clinician if it keeps happening."}],"instructions":"1. Make sure your nose is clear and breathing through it feels easy.\n2. Close your lips softly without pressing them together.\n3. Breathe in and out through your nose at an easy pace.\n4. If your nose is blocked or breathing feels hard, return to easy mouth breathing and see a clinician if it keeps happening.","safety_notes":"Never force nasal breathing or tape the mouth. Persistent mouth breathing, snoring or pauses in breathing at night need a medical assessment.","contraindications":["Asthma, heart or lung conditions: ask your clinician first","Pregnancy (avoid breath-holds)","Dizziness or fainting while practising","Blocked nose, or suspected sleep apnea: see a clinician"],"benefits":{"primary":"Quiet, comfortable breathing through the nose","secondary":["Relaxed jaw and face"]},"health_benefits":["Quiet, comfortable breathing through the nose","Relaxed jaw and face"],"tags":["oscar patel","nasal breathing"],"body_parts":["nose","diaphragm"],"recommended_duration":"Encouraged when the airway is clear","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":395},
{"id":"activity_oscar_fascia_pulling_thumb_on_palate_version","name":"Fascia Pulling (thumb-on-palate version)","category":"Recovery","domain":"grooming","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":false,"intensity":"low","description":"Oscar's website: lunge with the back heel lifted, thumb on the palate, then a head-spine-hips twist and back-heel pivot. The hands-free twist is #4., retained as research-only source material and not enabled for self-guided use.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"safety_notes":"Not available as a self-guided activity. Requires dental or orthodontic review before any implementation. The palate-thumb part is forceful manual pressure and is not an established treatment. The hands-free lunge twist is offered separately as #4.","contraindications":["Under 18","Dental work or orthodontics","TMJ symptoms","Oral injury or infection","Recent facial surgery"],"tags":["oscar patel","fascia pulling","research-only"],"body_parts":["mouth","palate","full_body"],"recommended_duration":"Hold a few seconds before rotating; no verified total count","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; nothing here is a recommendation to try it.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":382},
{"id":"activity_oscar_foot_ball_rolling","name":"Foot Ball Rolling","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Self-myofascial release","domain":"fitness","type":"canonical","verb":"Roll","lane_subcategory":"Rest","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Rolling the sole of the foot over a ball to release the fascia underneath.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Place the ball","instruction":"Put a ball under the sole of your foot, holding on to a wall or chair for balance."},{"order":2,"title":"Roll heel to toes","instruction":"Roll slowly from the heel toward the toes."},{"order":3,"title":"Cross the arch","instruction":"Move the ball across the arch and the ball of the foot."},{"order":4,"title":"Pause gently","instruction":"Pause on tight spots with light pressure."},{"order":5,"title":"Change foot","instruction":"Repeat on the other foot."}],"instructions":"1. Put a ball under the sole of your foot, holding on to a wall or chair for balance.\n2. Roll slowly from the heel toward the toes.\n3. Move the ball across the arch and the ball of the foot.\n4. Pause on tight spots with light pressure.\n5. Repeat on the other foot.","safety_notes":"Use light-to-moderate pressure, never directly on a joint or bone. Move slowly and stop if it is sharply painful.","contraindications":["Blood clot or circulation problems, or taking blood thinners, unless your clinician has cleared it","Open wounds, bruising, rash or skin infection at the spot","Sharp, shooting or nerve-type pain (stop; use a lighter touch or skip it)","Diabetic neuropathy or numb feet"],"benefits":{"primary":"Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","secondary":["Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"]},"health_benefits":["Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"],"tags":["oscar patel","fascia","self-massage"],"body_parts":["feet"],"equipment_needed":["ball or foam roller"],"equipment":["ball or foam roller"],"recommended_duration":"30–60 seconds per foot","recommended_frequency":"Daily or as needed","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":307},
{"id":"activity_oscar_forehead_and_scalp_release","name":"Forehead and Scalp Release","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Facial muscles","domain":"grooming","type":"canonical","verb":"Massage","lane_subcategory":"Hair/Grooming","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Gentle fingertip circles from the forehead over the scalp.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Start at the forehead","instruction":"Place your fingertips on your forehead."},{"order":2,"title":"Sweep to the hairline","instruction":"Massage from the forehead toward the hairline in gentle circles."},{"order":3,"title":"Spread across the scalp","instruction":"Spread your fingers across the scalp and continue with gentle circles."}],"instructions":"1. Place your fingertips on your forehead.\n2. Massage from the forehead toward the hairline in gentle circles.\n3. Spread your fingers across the scalp and continue with gentle circles.","safety_notes":"Use gentle pressure; stop if it is painful.","contraindications":["Skin infection, acne flare or open wounds in the area","Recent facial surgery, fillers or injectables","Eye conditions: never press on the eyeball","Scalp infection or open sores"],"benefits":{"primary":"Releases tension across the forehead and scalp","secondary":["Relaxation"]},"health_benefits":["Releases tension across the forehead and scalp","Relaxation"],"tags":["oscar patel","face","facial muscles","scalp"],"body_parts":["face","forehead"],"equipment_needed":["clean hands"],"equipment":["clean hands"],"recommended_duration":"About 60 seconds","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":360},
{"id":"activity_oscar_full_body_spiral_reaches","name":"Full-Body Spiral Reaches","category":"Fitness","subcategory":"Warm-up and movement","domain":"fitness","type":"canonical","verb":"Reach","lane_subcategory":"Yoga","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Diagonal reaches that let the chest, spine and hips follow one another.","duration_minutes":3,"default_duration_min":3,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Set your stance","instruction":"Stand with your feet hip-width apart."},{"order":2,"title":"Reach across","instruction":"Reach one arm diagonally across your body."},{"order":3,"title":"Let the spine follow","instruction":"Allow your chest and upper spine to follow the reach, and the opposite hip to rotate comfortably."},{"order":4,"title":"Return and switch","instruction":"Come back to centre and reach with the other arm."}],"instructions":"1. Stand with your feet hip-width apart.\n2. Reach one arm diagonally across your body.\n3. Allow your chest and upper spine to follow the reach, and the opposite hip to rotate comfortably.\n4. Come back to centre and reach with the other arm.","safety_notes":"Rotate only as far as is comfortable; do not force the spine or hips.","contraindications":["Acute injury, or pain that sharpens with the movement","Dizziness or balance problems (use a wall or chair for support)","Recent surgery, unless your clinician has cleared it"],"benefits":{"primary":"Opens up diagonal, spiral movement through the trunk","secondary":["Hip and thoracic mobility","Coordination between arms, spine and hips"]},"health_benefits":["Opens up diagonal, spiral movement through the trunk","Hip and thoracic mobility","Coordination between arms, spine and hips"],"tags":["oscar patel","warm-up","spiral","rotation"],"body_parts":["full_body","obliques","spine"],"recommended_duration":"10 reps in total (5 each side)","recommended_frequency":"Daily, as a warm-up","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public 