{"id":"activity_oscar_light_bouncing","name":"Light Bouncing","category":"Fitness","subcategory":"Warm-up and movement","domain":"fitness","type":"canonical","verb":"Bounce","lane_subcategory":"Walking","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"A gentle heel-bounce used as the opening warm-up of the routine.","duration_minutes":3,"default_duration_min":3,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Stand tall","instruction":"Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart and your shoulders relaxed."},{"order":2,"title":"Lift the heels","instruction":"Rise a little onto the balls of your feet."},{"order":3,"title":"Let them settle","instruction":"Let the heels drop and rebound in an easy rhythm, with soft knees."},{"order":4,"title":"Keep it light","instruction":"Stay relaxed through the shoulders and jaw; the bounce is small and quiet."}],"instructions":"1. Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart and your shoulders relaxed.\n2. Rise a little onto the balls of your feet.\n3. Let the heels drop and rebound in an easy rhythm, with soft knees.\n4. Stay relaxed through the shoulders and jaw; the bounce is small and quiet.","safety_notes":"Keep the bounce small and soft. Stop if you feel ankle, knee or back pain.","contraindications":["Acute injury, or pain that sharpens with the movement","Dizziness or balance problems (use a wall or chair for support)","Recent surgery, unless your clinician has cleared it"],"benefits":{"primary":"Wakes the body up before release and stretching work","secondary":["Light calf and ankle activation","Easy rhythm to loosen the shoulders"]},"health_benefits":["Wakes the body up before release and stretching work","Light calf and ankle activation","Easy rhythm to loosen the shoulders"],"tags":["oscar patel","warm-up","full body"],"body_parts":["full_body","calves"],"recommended_duration":"2–3 minutes","recommended_frequency":"Daily, as a warm-up","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":301},
{"id":"activity_oscar_lingual_frenulum_stimulation","name":"Lingual frenulum stimulation","category":"Recovery","domain":"grooming","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":false,"intensity":"low","description":"Manual stimulation beneath the tongue, retained as research-only source material and not enabled for self-guided use.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"safety_notes":"Not available as a self-guided activity. Requires dental or orthodontic review before any implementation. Pressure under the tongue can injure delicate tissue. Tongue-tie is assessed and treated by a qualified clinician.","contraindications":["Under 18","Dental work or orthodontics","TMJ symptoms","Oral injury or infection","Recent facial surgery"],"tags":["oscar patel","frenulum","research-only"],"body_parts":["mouth","tongue"],"recommended_duration":"30 seconds","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; nothing here is a recommendation to try it.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":387},
{"id":"activity_oscar_lip_press_resistance","name":"Lip-Press Resistance","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Tongue and swallowing","domain":"grooming","type":"canonical","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Holding a flat object between the lips and pressing them together.","duration_minutes":3,"default_duration_min":3,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Choose a safe object","instruction":"Use a large, flat, clean object that cannot slip into the mouth, such as a lip trainer or a wide spatula."},{"order":2,"title":"Hold with the lips only","instruction":"Hold it between your lips, not your teeth."},{"order":3,"title":"Press the lips together","instruction":"Press the lips together around it."},{"order":4,"title":"Release","instruction":"Let go and rest."}],"instructions":"1. Use a large, flat, clean object that cannot slip into the mouth, such as a lip trainer or a wide spatula.\n2. Hold it between your lips, not your teeth.\n3. Press the lips together around it.\n4. Let go and rest.","safety_notes":"Never use a small object such as a button or coin. Keep the object large and flat so it cannot be swallowed.","contraindications":["Dental work, braces or jaw (TMJ) pain: check with your dentist first","Difficulty swallowing or a choking risk","Oral injury, ulcers or infection","Under 18 unless a clinician has prescribed it","Any risk of swallowing or inhaling the object"],"benefits":{"primary":"Trains lip strength and seal","secondary":["Facial muscle endurance"]},"health_benefits":["Trains lip strength and seal","Facial muscle endurance"],"tags":["oscar patel","myofunctional","tongue","lips"],"body_parts":["mouth","tongue","jaw","lips"],"equipment_needed":["large flat lip trainer or wide spatula"],"equipment":["large flat lip trainer or wide spatula"],"recommended_duration":"10–20 second holds × 3","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Tongue and swallowing exercises taught by a clinician have trial evidence for sleep apnea (systematic review linked); the claim that tongue posture reshapes adult facial bone is not supported by good evidence. Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11793941/","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":346},
