{"id":"activity_oscar_macebell_spirals","name":"Macebell Spirals","category":"Fitness","subcategory":"Warm-up and movement","domain":"fitness","type":"canonical","verb":"Swing","lane_subcategory":"Strength","is_active":true,"intensity":"moderate","description":"Slow spirals and figure-eights with a light stick or macebell.","duration_minutes":5,"default_duration_min":5,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Rehearse unweighted","instruction":"Begin with an unweighted stick or broom handle to learn the pattern."},{"order":2,"title":"Slow side-to-side spirals","instruction":"Practise slow rotational swings from one shoulder to the other."},{"order":3,"title":"Progress to figure-eights","instruction":"Move on to smooth figure-eight patterns once the spirals are easy."},{"order":4,"title":"Keep joints easy","instruction":"Keep your wrists and shoulders comfortable throughout."},{"order":5,"title":"Reset","instruction":"Return to a neutral stance between sequences."}],"instructions":"1. Begin with an unweighted stick or broom handle to learn the pattern.\n2. Practise slow rotational swings from one shoulder to the other.\n3. Move on to smooth figure-eight patterns once the spirals are easy.\n4. Keep your wrists and shoulders comfortable throughout.\n5. Return to a neutral stance between sequences.","safety_notes":"Clear the space around you, use a light implement and add weight only gradually.","contraindications":["Acute injury, or pain that sharpens with the movement","Dizziness or balance problems (use a wall or chair for support)","Recent surgery, unless your clinician has cleared it","Shoulder, elbow or wrist injury"],"benefits":{"primary":"Teaches smooth rotational, spiral movement with the shoulders and trunk","secondary":["Grip and forearm endurance","Shoulder mobility"]},"health_benefits":["Teaches smooth rotational, spiral movement with the shoulders and trunk","Grip and forearm endurance","Shoulder mobility"],"tags":["oscar patel","macebell","spirals","rotation"],"body_parts":["shoulders","forearms","obliques","full_body"],"equipment_needed":["stick or light macebell"],"equipment":["stick or light macebell"],"recommended_duration":"2–3 sessions per week; no fixed reps","recommended_frequency":"2–3 times a week","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":305},
{"id":"activity_oscar_masseter_chewing","name":"Masseter Chewing","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Tongue and swallowing","domain":"grooming","type":"canonical","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Slow, thorough chewing with comfortable alternating jaw movement.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Take a small bite","instruction":"Take a small bite of food."},{"order":2,"title":"Chew slowly","instruction":"Chew slowly with a comfortable, alternating jaw movement."},{"order":3,"title":"Avoid clenching","instruction":"Avoid excessive clenching or very hard foods."},{"order":4,"title":"Count","instruction":"Aim for around 20–30 chews before swallowing."}],"instructions":"1. Take a small bite of food.\n2. Chew slowly with a comfortable, alternating jaw movement.\n3. Avoid excessive clenching or very hard foods.\n4. Aim for around 20–30 chews before swallowing.","safety_notes":"Do not clench. Stop if your jaw clicks painfully or tires.","contraindications":["Dental work, braces or jaw (TMJ) pain: check with your dentist first","Difficulty swallowing or a choking risk","Oral injury, ulcers or infection","Under 18 unless a clinician has prescribed it","Jaw pain or locking"],"benefits":{"primary":"Builds slow, thorough chewing habits","secondary":["Better digestion cues","Even use of both sides"]},"health_benefits":["Builds slow, thorough chewing habits","Better digestion cues","Even use of both sides"],"tags":["oscar patel","myofunctional","tongue","chewing","masseter"],"body_parts":["mouth","tongue","jaw","lips"],"recommended_duration":"Guide suggests 20–30 chews per bite","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Tongue and swallowing exercises taught by a clinician have trial evidence for sleep apnea (systematic review linked); the claim that tongue posture reshapes adult facial bone is not supported by good evidence. Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11793941/","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":351},
