{"id":"activity_oscar_middle_and_lower_trapezius_release","name":"Middle and Lower Trapezius Release","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Self-myofascial release","domain":"fitness","type":"canonical","verb":"Roll","lane_subcategory":"Rest","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"A ball on the wall between the shoulder blade and spine, rolled slowly along the muscle.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Position the ball","instruction":"Place a ball between your shoulder blade and your spine, against a wall."},{"order":2,"title":"Move slowly","instruction":"Roll slowly along the muscle by bending and straightening the knees."},{"order":3,"title":"Avoid the spine","instruction":"Keep the ball off the vertebrae themselves."}],"instructions":"1. Place a ball between your shoulder blade and your spine, against a wall.\n2. Roll slowly along the muscle by bending and straightening the knees.\n3. Keep the ball off the vertebrae themselves.","safety_notes":"Use light-to-moderate pressure, never directly on a joint or bone. Move slowly and stop if it is sharply painful.","contraindications":["Blood clot or circulation problems, or taking blood thinners, unless your clinician has cleared it","Open wounds, bruising, rash or skin infection at the spot","Sharp, shooting or nerve-type pain (stop; use a lighter touch or skip it)"],"benefits":{"primary":"Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","secondary":["Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"]},"health_benefits":["Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"],"tags":["oscar patel","fascia","self-massage"],"body_parts":["trapezius","middle_trapezius","back"],"equipment_needed":["ball or foam roller"],"equipment":["ball or foam roller"],"recommended_duration":"Within the trapezius session","recommended_frequency":"Daily or as needed","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips