{"id":"activity_oscar_neck_warm_up_rotation","name":"Neck Warm-up Rotation","category":"Stretch","subcategory":"Neck","domain":"fitness","type":"canonical","verb":"Turn","lane_subcategory":"Yoga","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Slow left-centre-right head turns to warm the neck up.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Sit tall","instruction":"Sit or stand tall with relaxed shoulders."},{"order":2,"title":"Turn left","instruction":"Turn your head gently toward the left."},{"order":3,"title":"Return to centre","instruction":"Come back to the middle."},{"order":4,"title":"Turn right","instruction":"Turn gently toward the right, without forcing a full circle."}],"instructions":"1. Sit or stand tall with relaxed shoulders.\n2. Turn your head gently toward the left.\n3. Come back to the middle.\n4. Turn gently toward the right, without forcing a full circle.","safety_notes":"Never force a full 360° circle or go to the end of the range.","contraindications":["Neck or arm pain, numbness or tingling","Dizziness, visual changes or faintness with neck movement","Recent neck injury or surgery","Known cervical spine or blood-vessel conditions"],"benefits":{"primary":"Gentle neck mobility","secondary":["Warm-up before neck work"]},"health_benefits":["Gentle neck mobility","Warm-up before neck work"],"tags":["oscar patel","neck","rotation"],"body_parts":["neck","cervical_spine"],"recommended_duration":"As comfortable","recommended_frequency":"3–4 sessions a week","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Low-load deep neck flexor training has trial evidence for neck pain (systematic review linked). Heavier neck loading is not covered here. Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6263552/","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":368},
{"id":"activity_oscar_orbicularis_oculi_activation","name":"Orbicularis Oculi Activation","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Facial muscles","domain":"grooming","type":"canonical","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"A light squeeze of the muscle ring around the eyes.","duration_minutes":3,"default_duration_min":3,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Close the lids","instruction":"Close your eyelids gently."},{"order":2,"title":"Squeeze lightly","instruction":"Squeeze lightly without wrinkling or pulling the skin."},{"order":3,"title":"Relax","instruction":"Release fully and open your eyes."}],"instructions":"1. Close your eyelids gently.\n2. Squeeze lightly without wrinkling or pulling the skin.\n3. Release fully and open your eyes.","safety_notes":"Keep it light; never press on the eyeball or pull the skin.","contraindications":["Skin infection, acne flare or open wounds in the area","Recent facial surgery, fillers or injectables","Eye conditions: never press on the eyeball","Glaucoma or recent eye surgery"],"benefits":{"primary":"Trains the muscle around the eye","secondary":["Eyelid control"]},"health_benefits":["Trains the muscle around the eye","Eyelid control"],"tags":["oscar patel","face","facial muscles"],"body_parts":["face","eyes"],"equipment_needed":["clean hands"],"equipment":["clean hands"],"recommended_duration":"Oscar describes 2 sets of 20","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":355},
{"id":"activity_oscar_orbicularis_oris_popping","name":"Orbicularis Oris Popping","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Facial muscles","domain":"grooming","type":"canonical","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Gentle cheek suction released with a soft lip pop.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Draw the cheeks in","instruction":"Draw your cheeks gently inward."},{"order":2,"title":"Create suction","instruction":"Close the lips to make a light suction."},{"order":3,"title":"Release with a pop","instruction":"Release the lips so they pop softly."},{"order":4,"title":"Reset","instruction":"Relax your face between reps."}],"instructions":"1. Draw your cheeks gently inward.\n2. Close the lips to make a light suction.\n3. Release the lips so they pop softly.\n4. Relax your face between reps.","safety_notes":"Light effort only; stop if your jaw or cheeks hurt.","contraindications":["Skin infection, acne flare or open wounds in the area","Recent facial surgery, fillers or injectables","Eye conditions: never press on the eyeball"],"benefits":{"primary":"Trains the muscle ring around the mouth","secondary":["Lip and cheek control"]},"health_benefits":["Trains the muscle ring around the mouth","Lip and cheek control"],"tags":["oscar patel","face","facial muscles"],"body_parts":["face","lips","cheeks","mouth"],"equipment_needed":["clean hands"],"equipment":["clean hands"],"recommended_duration":"2 sets of 10","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":354},
{"id":"activity_oscar_orbicularis_tapping","name":"Orbicularis Tapping","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Facial muscles","domain":"grooming","type":"canonical","verb":"Tap","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Very light tapping over the brow and outer orbital bone.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Find the bone","instruction":"Locate the bony ridge around your eye socket."},{"order":2,"title":"Tap lightly","instruction":"Tap very lightly over the brow and the outer edge of the orbital bone."},{"order":3,"title":"Avoid the eyeball","instruction":"Never press on the eye itself."}],"instructions":"1. Locate the bony ridge around your eye socket.\n2. Tap very lightly over the brow and the outer edge of the orbital bone.\n3. Never press on the eye itself.","safety_notes":"Keep the taps feather-light and well away from the eyeball.","contraindications":["Skin infection, acne flare or open wounds in the area","Recent facial surgery, fillers or injectables","Eye conditions: never press on the eyeball","Glaucoma or recent eye surgery"],"benefits":{"primary":"Gentle stimulation of the area around the eyes","secondary":["Facial awareness"]},"health_benefits":["Gentle stimulation of the area around the eyes","Facial awareness"],"tags":["oscar patel","face","facial muscles","tapping"],"body_parts":["face","eyes","forehead"],"equipment_needed":["clean hands"],"equipment":["clean hands"],"recommended_duration":"Not specified","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":359},
{"id":"activity_oscar_palate_massage","name":"Palate massage","category":"Recovery","domain":"grooming","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":false,"intensity":"low","description":"Back-to-front manual sweeping along the hard palate, retained as research-only source material and not enabled for self-guided use.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"safety_notes":"Not available as a self-guided activity. Requires dental or orthodontic review before any implementation. Manual pressure inside the mouth can injure tissue and is not an established treatment.","contraindications":["Under 18","Dental work or orthodontics","TMJ symptoms","Oral injury or infection","Recent facial surgery"],"tags":["oscar patel","palate","research-only"],"body_parts":["mouth","palate"],"recommended_duration":"30–60 seconds","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; nothing here is a recommendation to try it.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":384},
{"id":"activity_oscar_pectoral_release","name":"Pectoral Release","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Self-myofascial release","domain":"fitness","type":"canonical","verb":"Roll","lane_subcategory":"Rest","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"A soft ball against a wall to release the chest muscle near the shoulder.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Set a soft ball on the wall","instruction":"Place a soft ball between the wall and the muscle of your chest near the shoulder."},{"order":2,"title":"Make small movements","instruction":"Lean in lightly and make small horizontal and vertical movements."},{"order":3,"title":"Change side","instruction":"Repeat on the other side."}],"instructions":"1. Place a soft ball between the wall and the muscle of your chest near the shoulder.\n2. Lean in lightly and make small horizontal and vertical movements.\n3. Repeat on the other side.","safety_notes":"Use light-to-moderate pressure, never directly on a joint or bone. Move slowly and stop if it is sharply painful.","contraindications":["Blood clot or circulation problems, or taking blood thinners, unless your clinician has cleared it","Open wounds, bruising, rash or skin infection at the spot","Sharp, shooting or nerve-type pain (stop; use a lighter touch or skip it)","Recent chest or breast surgery","Pacemaker or implanted device near the area"],"benefits":{"primary":"Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","secondary":["Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"]},"health_benefits":["Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"],"tags":["oscar patel","fascia","self-massage"],"body_parts":["chest","pectorals"],"equipment_needed":["ball or foam roller"],"equipment":["ball or foam roller"],"recommended_duration":"60 seconds per side","recommended_frequency":"Daily or as needed","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":312},
{"id":"activity_oscar_proper_swallowing","name":"Proper Swallowing","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Tongue and swallowing","domain":"grooming","type":"canonical","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Swallowing with the tongue leading and the cheeks and chin staying quiet.","duration_minutes":1,"default_duration_min":1,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Keep the lips relaxed","instruction":"Let the lips rest together without squeezing."},{"order":2,"title":"Let the tongue lead","instruction":"Let the tongue move the food or saliva backward."},{"order":3,"title":"Avoid extra effort","instruction":"Avoid unnecessary tension in the cheeks and chin."}],"instructions":"1. Let the lips rest together without squeezing.\n2. Let the tongue move the food or saliva backward.\n3. Avoid unnecessary tension in the cheeks and chin.","safety_notes":"Do not force or exaggerate a swallow. See a speech-language pathologist for swallowing difficulty.","contraindications":["Dental work, braces or jaw (TMJ) pain: check with your dentist first","Difficulty swallowing or a choking risk","Oral injury, ulcers or infection","Under 18 unless a clinician has prescribed it"],"benefits":{"primary":"Awareness of a relaxed swallow","secondary":["Less cheek and chin tension"]},"health_benefits":["Awareness of a relaxed swallow","Less cheek and chin tension"],"tags":["oscar patel","myofunctional","tongue","swallow"],"body_parts":["mouth","tongue","jaw","lips"],"recommended_duration":"With normal swallowing","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Tongue and swallowing exercises taught by a clinician have trial evidence for sleep apnea (systematic review linked); the claim that tongue posture reshapes adult facial bone is not supported by good evidence. Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11793941/","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":349},
{"id":"activity_oscar_psoas_release_deep_abdominal_pressure","name":"Psoas Release (deep abdominal pressure)","category":"Recovery","domain":"grooming","verb":"Release","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":false,"intensity":"low","description":"Oscar-community guide describes deep abdominal pressure near the front hip bone to reach the psoas muscle, retained as research-only source material and not enabled for self-guided use.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"safety_notes":"Not available as a self-guided activity. Requires dental or orthodontic review before any implementation. Pressing deeply into the abdomen to find the psoas is not a safe general self-massage technique: the abdomen holds nerves, blood vessels and organs. A half-kneeling hip-flexor stretch (#21) is the safer starting point.","contraindications":["Under 18","Dental work or orthodontics","TMJ symptoms","Oral injury or infection","Recent facial surgery"],"tags":["oscar patel","psoas","research-only"],"body_parts":["hip_flexors","abdomen"],"recommended_duration":"60–90 seconds per side","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; nothing here is a recommendation to try it.","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":318},
{"id":"activity_oscar_pursed_lip_breathing","name":"Pursed-Lip Breathing","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Tongue and swallowing","domain":"grooming","type":"canonical","verb":"Practice","lane_subcategory":"Jaw exercises","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Slow breaths out through relaxed, pursed lips.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Breathe in","instruction":"Inhale gently through your nose."},{"order":2,"title":"Purse the lips","instruction":"Form a relaxed, narrow opening with your lips."},{"order":3,"title":"Breathe out slowly","instruction":"Breathe out slowly through the pursed lips."}],"instructions":"1. Inhale gently through your nose.\n2. Form a relaxed, narrow opening with your lips.\n3. Breathe out slowly through the pursed lips.","safety_notes":"Keep it relaxed and never force the breath. Stop if you feel dizzy.","contraindications":["Dental work, braces or jaw (TMJ) pain: check with your dentist first","Difficulty swallowing or a choking risk","Oral injury, ulcers or infection","Under 18 unless a clinician has prescribed it","Lung conditions: follow your clinician's breathing advice"],"benefits":{"primary":"Slows the breath and relaxes the face","secondary":["Lip control"]},"health_benefits":["Slows the breath and relaxes the face","Lip control"],"tags":["oscar patel","myofunctional","tongue","breathing","lips"],"body_parts":["mouth","tongue","jaw","lips"],"recommended_duration":"Not consistently specified","recommended_frequency":"Daily","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Tongue and swallowing exercises taught by a clinician have trial evidence for sleep apnea (systematic review linked); the claim that tongue posture reshapes adult facial bone is not supported by good evidence. Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 October 2026 from his website, videos, social posts and an unverified community document; the steps are a practical adaptation, not word-for-word instructions.","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11793941/","is_group":false,"is_prenatal":false,"target_gender":["all"],"target_age_min":18,"sort_order":348},
{"id":"activity_oscar_quadriceps_release","name":"Quadriceps Release","category":"Recovery","subcategory":"Self-myofascial release","domain":"fitness","type":"canonical","verb":"Roll","lane_subcategory":"Rest","is_active":true,"intensity":"low","description":"Rolling the front of the thigh, below the hip to above the knee.","duration_minutes":2,"default_duration_min":2,"steps":[{"order":1,"title":"Lie face down","instruction":"Lie face down with the roller under the front of one thigh, forearms supporting you."},{"order":2,"title":"Roll","instruction":"Roll from just below the hip to just above the knee. Avoid pressing on the kneecap or joint."},{"order":3,"title":"Switch","instruction":"Repeat on the other thigh."}],"instructions":"1. Lie face down with the roller under the front of one thigh, forearms supporting you.\n2. Roll from just below the hip to just above the knee. Avoid pressing on the kneecap or joint.\n3. Repeat on the other thigh.","safety_notes":"Use light-to-moderate pressure, never directly on a joint or bone. Move slowly and stop if it is sharply painful.","contraindications":["Blood clot or circulation problems, or taking blood thinners, unless your clinician has cleared it","Open wounds, bruising, rash or skin infection at the spot","Sharp, shooting or nerve-type pain (stop; use a lighter touch or skip it)"],"benefits":{"primary":"Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","secondary":["Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"]},"health_benefits":["Eases tension in the area before stretching and strengthening","Body awareness","Short, easy recovery habit"],"tags":["oscar patel","fascia","self-massage"],"body_parts":["quadriceps","legs"],"equipment_needed":["ball or foam roller"],"equipment":["ball or foam roller"],"recommended_duration":"30 seconds per side","recommended_frequency":"Daily or as needed","recommended_intensity":"Comfortable and pain-free","tips":"Described in Oscar Patel's public materials as compiled on 25 